: "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Activity 2", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Origins of Programming Languages", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear to talk about programming languages", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify information about the history of software and its characteristics in simple spoken and written situations. Give information about software history, characteristics and methodologies", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Tense of Verb Be - Was in Negative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>Use the <strong>simple past</strong> to talk about events that started and finished in the past.</p> <p>You can use the <strong>verb to be</strong> in the <strong>simple past</strong> to describe events in the past about characteristic, places, or locations.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>To make a <strong>negative</strong> statement with the <strong>verb to be</strong> in the <strong>simple past</strong>, use the following structure:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>was </strong>/ <strong>were</strong> + <strong>not</strong> + complement</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>COBOL <strong>was not</strong> easy to use.</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Use <strong>was</strong> with <strong>I</strong>, <strong>he</strong>, <strong>she</strong> and <strong>it</strong>; use <strong>were</strong> with <strong>you</strong>, <strong>we</strong> and <strong>they</strong>.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>You can also use contracted forms:</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>In the past, computers <strong>weren&rsquo;t</strong> machines but people who worked out mathematical problems.</i></p> <p><i>Software <strong>wasn&rsquo;t</strong> a common term in the 50s.</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Did you know that the word software wasn't used before 1958?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The word computer was not related to electronic machines but for people who work out mathematical problems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There was not any difference between systems and applications software.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "FORTRAN", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p><strong>FORTRAN</strong> is a procedural, vital, compiled language with a syntax well suited that represents mathematical formulas.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>IBM created <strong>FORTRAN</strong>, which stands for<i> Formula Translation,</i> in the 1950s for scientific and engineering applications. This programming language came to dominate the area of programming, and actually, it continues in diverse areas like numerical weather prediction, finite element analysis, computational fluid dynamics, computational physics, crystallography, and computational chemistry.</p> <p><strong>FORTRAN</strong> keeps on incorporating new and better versions. Each has evolved to add extensions to the language and retaining compatibility with prior versions.</p>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "programming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the process of writing software codes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am reading about the history of programming languages and operating systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "true", "type": "name"}, {"content": "real; genuine or authentic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first true operating system was MAD, which stands for Michigan Algorithmic Decoder.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "enable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give power or authorize someone to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: 3GLs enabled programs to be hierarchical and structured.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "derive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to come from", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This operating system derives from ALGOL.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "point the way ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show the way to get somewhere", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Her work pointed the way to the development of FORTRAN.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "a)\tLook for further information about third generation languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b)\tWrite three characteristics of a modern third generation language. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "c)\tRead that brief text to your teacher. Be careful with the pronunciation. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "\u274f\tI look for more information about third generation languages. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\u274f\tI identify some characteristics of third generation languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\u274f\tI share the information and practice pronunciation in class. ", "type": "text"}]}]}